  "symbols": {
    "units": "m",
    "why": "Legend: overlined red numbers are depths in metres, blue R restrictions, a blue wavy line with an arrowhead the flow. The figure is small (0.6 m/px) and its red digits defeat OCR: every depth was located by its red ink and read by eye on zoomed crops (letters and numbers detection off: 'letters' empty, the OCR's 25 misread numbers dropped with 'fix'); the R's placed by eye. Flow: only the six wavy arrows whose head is legible (four in Sagitario's central room, heading south to south-south-east, two in La Mina's south-west passage); others in La Mina's grey are too small to read. Not kept: the sample stations S1-S20 (red dots) and the figure references (2D, 3A...) with their leaders - the article's, not the cave's; no bones or 'To ...' pointers on the map. Place names: La Mina (the mining section); Sagitario, Pu'bix and Kilix Pach-Och are the entrances.",
